{%- comment -%}
  A page's hero or page header, from the page's own fields (content model parts 1 and 6, DS-14):
  hero image, whether it is an artwork, label, intro, call to action, caption. A page with a hero
  image gets the hero (DESIGN.md §6.3); a page without one gets the page header (§6.6), so a weak
  image is never stretched into a hero. Nothing here is a section setting, so one template serves
  many pages without their content leaking into each other (L-01).

  A programme page's logo is in the header (DS-47), so the page header doesn't repeat it. No logo
  ever sits in the title box: a boxed logo on its own box colour is not allowed (§8.3).

  The hero image takes its alt text from Files. Without one it is decorative, not the page title
  again: the title comes right after it (DS-58). An artwork's caption follows the work in the
  markup, before the box, so it reads and tabs in the order it shows; a photo's comes after the box.

  A programme in the events switcher gets the page header, as the Upcoming events page has, so the
  row of links stays in one place from view to view; its picture sits beside its words instead
  (gs-page-body, DS-146).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign f = page.metafields.custom
  assign image = f.hero_image.value
  if image != blank
    capture filtered
      render 'gs-programme-index', check: page
    endcapture
    if filtered contains 'true'
      assign image = nil
    endif
  endif
  assign mode = 'photo'
  if f.hero_is_artwork.value == true
    assign mode = 'artwork'
  endif
  assign cta = f.cta.value
  # An eyebrow that names another page links back to it (DS-80, Proposed): "Artists in Residence"
  # on a residency page is the Artists-in-Residence page.
  assign eyebrow = f.eyebrow.value | strip
  assign back = nil
  if eyebrow != blank
    assign back_handle = eyebrow | handleize
    assign back = pages[back_handle]
  endif
-%}
{%- if image != blank -%}
  <div class="gs-section gs-section--lead">
    <div class="gs-hero{% if mode == 'artwork' %} gs-hero--artwork{% endif %}"{% if mode == 'artwork' and image.aspect_ratio %} style="--gs-art-ratio: {{ image.aspect_ratio }}"{% endif %}>
      {%- capture caption -%}
        {%- if f.hero_caption.value != blank -%}
          <p class="gs-hero__caption gs-caption">{{ f.hero_caption.value | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- render 'gs-media', image: image, preset: 'hero', mode: mode, shape: 'lg', class: 'gs-hero__media' -%}
      {%- if mode == 'artwork' -%}{{ caption }}{%- endif -%}
      <div class="gs-hero__box gs-surface-accent">
        {%- render 'gs-title-block', title: page.title, eyebrow: eyebrow, back: back, deck: f.intro.value, cta: cta -%}
      </div>
      {%- if request.design_mode and mode == 'photo' and image.width < 1600 -%}
        <p class="gs-editor-warning">This photo is {{ image.width }} px wide. A hero photo needs 1600 px or more to look sharp on large screens: use a larger copy, or remove it to show the page header.</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if mode != 'artwork' -%}{{ caption }}{%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="gs-container gs-lead-in">
    <header class="gs-page-head">
      {%- render 'gs-title-block', title: page.title, eyebrow: eyebrow, back: back, deck: f.intro.value, cta: cta -%}
    </header>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Page hero or header",
  "tag": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["page"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Everything here comes from the page's own fields, at the bottom of the page in Online Store, Pages: Hero image, Hero is artwork, Eyebrow, Intro, Call to action, Hero caption and Programme. Without a hero image the page gets a plain header."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Page hero or header"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
